post.description:
Dispatch the selected metadata button payload as a twin command.

Sends MQTT command:
    {"command": "button", "data": <metadata.buttons[button_index].payload>}

Fetch a fresh token and, if already registered, re-verify — never
(re-)registers. `status` only becomes CONNECTED if verify() actually ran;
a successful token fetch alone just means credentials still work.

MLTrainingMetricsUpdateSchema.description:
Schema for updating training metrics logs.

Used when updating training metrics via PUT /mltrainings/{uuid}/metrics
This allows logging multiple steps at once or single step updates.

Payload options:
- Single step: {"step": 100, "log": {"loss": 0.5}, "eta": "...", "loss": 0.5}
- Multiple steps: {"logs": [{"step": 100, "log": {...}, ...}, ...]}
